# L §6.1: the joint model "may add items of its own (kinds, defs, versions, asks); it never changes an imported one";
# a row of its own on a member's item settles two rows stated same. Its row on b.rent_in[2026-04], which no same line
# joins, would change an imported item. Round 14 (L §6.1 The joint model's own rows): "of a member's item only at a
# pair stated same ...; a row or an entry of any other member's item would change an imported one, and is refused
# (LOAD-SAME)"; L §8.3: "the joint model states <x>[k], an item of member <a> that no same line joins". (Writer 7.)
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "e42519b086605a071d9ecc73cede5a0d6c7a969e069b921d3607f5353dd04a6c"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "0100e9a6e9d46e4f564190c5f45cf81d6966cbd6c5a95b32effabbaea4534b0d"
  same a.rent[2026-03] = b.rent_in[2026-03]

source joint_s "ustalenie"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

version settle
  cite joint_s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-02
  b.rent_in[2026-04] = 2 050.00 PLN "aneks"

ask ra: a.rent[2026-03]
ask rb: b.rent_in[2026-03]
ask r4: b.rent_in[2026-04]
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input rent[m in months]: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  rent[2026-03] = 2 000.00 PLN "umowa najmu"
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input rent_in[m in months]: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  rent_in[2026-03] = 2 100.00 PLN "umowa najmu"
  rent_in[2026-04] = 2 100.00 PLN "umowa najmu"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-SAME the joint model states b.rent_in[2026-04], an item of member b that no same line joins ...
